## Lore

The Fallam are big, minor Mega-Damage aliens whom the Arkhons conquered
centuries ago. Slaves at first and then second-class citizens, they were in
time accepted as full members of Arkhon society, and they grew close to clan
Tlo-Arkhon. When that clan went into exile on Earth, some four hundred thousand
Fallam warriors and their families followed; about 120,000 came through the
failed invasion and now serve the Arkhons of the Andes.

A Fallam stands seven to nine feet tall, with huge shoulders, a pinched waist,
short legs and long arms - their distant ancestors went on all fours, and they
still like to lean on their knuckles. Their skin is reddish-brown and their
pale hair grows in ragged tufts; a fin and two bony ridges run down the back of
the neck. They come from a jungle world and once built a civilization nearly as
advanced as pre-Rifts Earth, and they were a peaceable people until centuries
under the Arkhons made them as warlike and competitive as their masters.

Most Fallam on Earth share the Arkhons'' contempt for humans, and every Fallam
of Tlo-Arkhon is a soldier with a technical specialty. A few are dissidents
who long for independence: some desert and flee as far as they can, one band
reaching a D-bee village near Tolkeen, while others quietly sabotage Arkhon
operations - a hatch left open, a component that fails at the worst moment.
They are sometimes mistaken for the Red Giants.

## GM Notes

About 3% of the Fallam can enter the Battle Trance and are trained as
Battlemasters (see that O.C.C.). Even renegade Fallam are distrusted or hunted
by the peoples of South America.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'fallam');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'fallam';

